  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/083X">Lemma <span data-tag="083X">71.6.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X' \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $Z \subset X$ be a locally principal closed subspace. Then the inverse image $f^{-1}(Z)$ is a locally principal closed subspace of $X'$. </p>
